Z||000000||doughboySE||07-15-2000||09:47 PM||||for the last bit the car has alot of probs starting i think its the battery because when i turn the key there is nothing but if i turn the lights on or the radio and give it a sec it will start but takes a bit like a dieing battery.<BR>when i get to work and turn it off (45 km drive)and try to start it again its dead, but after sitting for the day when i go to go home its the same as in the morning but it will eventually start?<BR>the batter is only reg 10 volt and the starter and alternator were checked and are ok .<BR>my question is will a new battery solve this or could it be more? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||07-16-2000||12:29 AM||||   Doughboy, You'll never know untill you change the battery. While you have it running, take it to a auto parts store and have them check your charging system. They should be able to narrow it down for you. Remember to keep it running.<P>  Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Taijiguy||07-16-2000||07:49 AM||||If it will only start with the lights or radio on, that's one of those geeky kinds of things that makes me go looking for a ground problem. Maybe even a dirty battery contact, which, if you replace the battery, will get cleaned anyway. Dirty contacts and/or a poor ground connection will make a car do really odd things, since the ground is seeking all kinds of paths to do it's job (least resistance and all) and can send gauges, and lights and stuff into frenzied spasms of wierdness.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||07-16-2000||07:54 AM||||Last summer Ogre was famous for telling everyone to check all connections, grounds, and especially the little red wire that is attached to the positive terminal.||||reg||1
